				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Fire onFileSystem activation on register_file_system_provider\n\nExtract `register_file_system_provider` from the catch-all handler group and give it a dedicated match arm that fires `$activateByEvent(\"onFileSystem:{scheme}\")` when an extension registers a virtual file-system provider. The scheme is read from the `scheme` key in the parameters object.\n\nThis ensures extensions declaring `\"activationEvents\": [\"onFileSystem:xyz\"]` in their manifest are activated on registration, matching VS Code's behaviour. The provider is still forwarded through `RegisterLanguageProvider` for handle tracking, and a warning is logged when the provider falls outside the known language-feature map.",
			"SHA": "9f2f1783e8d68a4825ed628969e4297d12606d05"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:23:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Fix indentation of diagnostic:getBootMarks match arm in DispatchMatch\n\nThe `diagnostic:getBootMarks` handler and its preceding doc comment were indented one tab level deeper than the surrounding match arms in `mountain_ipc_invoke`, creating an inconsistent brace depth relative to the other cases.\n\nDedent the arm and comment block by one level to align with the enclosing match statement's formatting. No behavioral change.",
			"SHA": "9262422ce1ef71be84be4d5edeafe56025bdba8e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:23:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				12
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add language provider cancellation, decoration lazy-registration, and window event bridging\n\nImplement a cancellation system for language provider requests: store `watch::Sender<bool>` in the new `LanguageProviderCancellations` DashMap, keyed by renderer-supplied `requestId`, so that `language:cancelRequest` flips the sender locally instead of forwarding to Cocoon. Wire cancellation through `InvokeProvider` and `InvokeProviderMethod` by passing the cancellations map into `ForwardCancellable`.\n\nAdd lazy-decoration-type registration to `SetTextEditorDecorations`: when `decorationTypeKey` isn't in `KnownTypeKeys`, auto-forward a synthetic `createTextEditorDecorationType` to Sky so Monaco has styling registered before `setDecorationsByType` executes. Track known keys via `IsTypeKeyKnown` / `RegisterTypeKey` on `DecorationsState`.\n\nEmit `sky://window/maximize-changed` on maximize/unmaximize handlers and bridge `nativeHost:onDidChangeMaximizeState` from Cocoon to Sky. Emit `sky://storage/changed` on storage IPC handlers and `sky://webview/ready` on `WebviewReady` gRPC notification for reactive workbench consumers.\n\nSplit file-system IPC into its own `TierFileSystem` env var so `file:*` commands don't route to Cocoon (which has no disk provider). Replace the blocking 3-second `WaitForClientConnection` in `forward_to_cocoon` with a non-blocking `IsClientConnected` check, returning Null fallback when Cocoon is disconnected.\n\nForward `CommandNotFound` errors from Mountain's command registry to Cocoon's extension host via `proxy_cocoon` for both `executeCommand` and `commands:execute` paths, so palette-invoked extension commands that never reached Mountain's registry still execute.\n\nAdd `$acceptModelSaved` notification on `textFile:save` so `onDidSaveTextDocument` fires for extensions. Query real dirty URIs from `WorkingCopy::GetAllDirty` in `workspaces:getDirtyWorkspaces` instead of returning an empty array. Add empty-store short-circuit in `StorageGet` to skip trait dispatch on first boot. Raise gRPC connect initial delay from 50ms to 200ms matching real Cocoon bind times.\n\nLog unroutable `register_*` provider notifications on the gRPC service and return `false` instead of silently dropping them. Include `viewType` in `WebviewReady` log output.",
			"SHA": "d1c2117a977bec02903d935702d30d37f4b0376b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T20:37:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Route nativeHost picker to correct dialog type via options\n\nRead `canSelectFiles` and `canSelectFolders` from the options object passed by VS Code extensions in the `nativeHost:pickFolderAndOpen` handler, then route to `blocking_pick_folder` or `blocking_pick_file` accordingly. Previously the handler always opened a folder picker regardless of the caller's declared selection constraints.\n\nWhen neither flag is set (e.g. `canSelectFiles: false, canSelectFolders: false`) the handler returns early as cancelled, matching Electron's behaviour. Adds dev_log output for the resolved picker type.",
			"SHA": "042dd2ddc3e825e506478afbe872243d772e8cab"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T20:34:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Replace em dashes with hyphens in README.md\n\nConsistently replace all em dash characters (`—`) with standard hyphens (`-`) throughout the README.md, affecting the Feature list, Architecture table, Dependencies table, Security table, and Related Documentation links. The change moves from typographic punctuation to plain ASCII for consistency with the surrounding codebase documentation conventions.\n\nNo behavioral or semantic changes — prose style alignment only.",
			"SHA": "c8f239f13c0c09ef81f4d73cf9180e840f67beed"
		}
